WEBVTT

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:06.004
[grunts] As I was saying,

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:08.882
on the outside,
the five of you are villains,

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:11.051
predators,
remorseless sociopaths.

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:13.011
Oh, stop,
you're makin' me blush.

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:15.055
But inside, there's a flower.

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:16.849
The flower of goodness.

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.225
And when it blooms

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:22.312
and you feel that tingle of positivity
radiating through your body,

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:25.274
you're going to want to feel it
all the time.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.025
So, we're going for a tingle?

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.360
Not any tingle.

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:29.945
The tingle of goodness.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:34.199
Which you'll feel
in my state-of-the-art Sharing Laboratory!

00:00:34.951 --> 00:00:37.995
Okay, Mr. Snake,
I'm going to give you a Push Pop.

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:40.622
Great! Push Pop just for me!

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.291
No, to share.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.375
Why?

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.502
Well, on a fundamental level,

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:48.756
it's about putting someone else's needs
ahead of your own.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.840
[chuckling]

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:51.550
Oh, no. No way.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:52.801
Snake...

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:56.221
[sighs] All right, all right.

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:58.432
This is gonna taste extra sweet,

00:00:58.516 --> 00:01:00.976
'cause I know how bad you want it.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.520
[groaning]

00:01:03.605 --> 00:01:05.981
Pop me, please. Ah!

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.524
[groaning]

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.652
Nope!

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.405
- Sucker!
- That's it! I'll teach you to share!

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.407
[all gasp]

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:17.659
I like sharin'. It's yummy. Mmm.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.661
[Snake] Totally worth it.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.830
Well, that's terrifying.

00:01:22.332 --> 00:01:24.041
Let's try something simpler.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:28.003
A good person always pays attention
to the needs of others.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.631
Now, here's a kindly, frail grandma.

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:33.217
[all laughing]

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:36.303
Mr. Piranha,
help Grandma across the street.

00:01:36.387 --> 00:01:38.680
Pish! Sure, sure, sure.
I do this all the time.

00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:41.141
Here you go, ma'am.

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:42.601
[laughing]

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:44.561
Oh, he is totally gonna blow it.

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:46.897
- What was that? What did you say?
- [Tarantula laughing]

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:48.941
- You think I can't do this?
- No, no, no, Piranha...

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:50.025
[horn honking]

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.319
[Wolf screaming, grunts]

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.072
Maybe simpler?

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:56.782
[cat meowing]

00:01:56.866 --> 00:02:00.160
Hey, look!
It's a cat stuck in a tree.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:02.037
It doesn't get much simpler than that.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:06.166
Now, what in this scenario
would give you that good tingle?

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:10.003
Eating it? This is why I always carry
two pieces of bread with me.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:13.882
No. I want you to s...

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.092
- Smack it.
- Skin it?

00:02:15.176 --> 00:02:16.009
Stab it.

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:17.094
- Sauté it.
- Sing to it?

00:02:17.178 --> 00:02:19.429
Save it. I want you to save...

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.890
It's so obvious... I want you to save it.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.309
[all] Oh! Right, right.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.813
[all] Here, kitty, kitty cat!

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:28.897
[cat meowing]

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.275
Whoa,
that cat is obviously defective.

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:34.361
What is wrong with you?
You're gonna give it a heart attack.

00:02:34.445 --> 00:02:35.821
I'll handle this.

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:37.823
What's up, papa!

00:02:40.243 --> 00:02:42.286
- [yowling]
- Get him off my face! He's on my face!

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.372
No, no, no! Listen.
What are you doing?

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.334
[Wolf groaning]

00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:53.797
Okay. What, may I ask, are you good at?

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:56.800
- Stealing stuff?
- Oh, yeah, we're great at that.

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:57.926
- Robbery.
- Larceny.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.052
- Wire fraud.
- Extortion.

00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:00.304
- Tax evasion.
- Heists.

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:02.431
- [Tarantula] Mail fraud.
- Wait. "Heists," you say?

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.766
Well, that's...
Yeah, that's kind of our specialty.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.436
I might just have an idea.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.939
[protestors] Free the pigs! Free the pigs!

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.025
That is an animal testing lab.

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:16.236
Within, 200,000 helpless guinea pigs,

00:03:16.321 --> 00:03:20.282
all being poked and prodded
by sadistic scientists.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.742
Guinea pigs, you say?

00:03:21.826 --> 00:03:23.160
Snake...

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:24.578
I want you to rescue them.

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:26.830
But this is a heist for good.

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:30.208
So, I brought something
more friendly for you to wear.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:31.501
Bye.

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:34.338
Well, there goes our street cred.

00:03:35.006 --> 00:03:36.214
At least it's comfy.

00:03:38.176 --> 00:03:40.802
[Wolf] All right,
we need to distract that scientist.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.013
- Shark, you're up.
- Copy that.

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:45.515
Okay. We're gonna need
a rope and a hook.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.683
I got this one.

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:47.851
- What?
- You're volunteering?

00:03:47.936 --> 00:03:49.895
You've never volunteered
for anything.

00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:51.980
Sure I did. Right now.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.650
- Throw me up there! Giddy up!
- Really?

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.319
Yep.
I'm 99%_ sure you can make it.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.154
- Okay.
- Let's do it!

00:04:00.281 --> 00:04:02.491
- Hey there, son.
- Dad?

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.284
I know you've got an important job,

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:06.787
but I hope you still have time
for a catch with your old man.

00:04:06.871 --> 00:04:08.580
- [gasps]
- [Snake groans]

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:10.332
- Hey, kiddo.
- [Snake] 96%_ sure.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.292
You'll always be my special boy.

00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:14.962
[groans] Maybe 90%.

00:04:15.046 --> 00:04:17.714
I've been waiting my entire life
for this moment.

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:19.800
- Okay, then. Now, go long.
- [Snake] Ow! I don't know.

00:04:19.884 --> 00:04:22.552
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy!
Thank you, Daddy!

00:04:22.637 --> 00:04:23.845
[laughing]

00:04:24.681 --> 00:04:26.932
Ow! Fifty? What day is it?

00:04:27.016 --> 00:04:28.475
[Snake] Who am I?

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:32.312
Right. The guinea pigs are locked
behind a three-foot thick steel door.

00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:34.189
The only way in
is through the vents.

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:35.941
I got it.

00:04:36.025 --> 00:04:37.317
Upsy-daisy!

00:04:37.402 --> 00:04:38.860
<i>♪ Over the filters</i>
<i>And through the vents... ♪</i>

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:41.655
I have never seen him so chipper.
Has he been meditating?

00:04:41.739 --> 00:04:44.157
<i>♪ To Guinea Pig Land we... ♪</i>

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:45.409
[Snake screams]

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:47.786
- [squeaking]
- [groans]

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.621
[slurping]

00:04:50.331 --> 00:04:51.748
Oh.

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:53.959
[whispering] Snake attack.

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.419
[protestors chanting]

00:04:55.503 --> 00:04:57.004
Hey, look! It's Professor Marmalade.

00:04:57.088 --> 00:05:00.841
Yes, that's right.
It's me. Help has arrived.

00:05:00.925 --> 00:05:03.260
Just keep your eyes glued to that door.

00:05:03.845 --> 00:05:05.595
Snake. Come on, Snake, open up.

00:05:06.222 --> 00:05:09.683
Relax. These doors are complicated.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.768
- [Tarantula] Are you kidding me?
- [guinea pigs squealing]

00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:13.186
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:15.147
We're supposed to save them,
not eat them.

00:05:15.231 --> 00:05:17.858
Well, I'd say
they've gone to a better place.

00:05:17.942 --> 00:05:18.942
[burps, laughs]

00:05:19.027 --> 00:05:20.193
That's it.

00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:21.903
Spit them out!

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:25.198
We're gonna save you
whether you like it or not.

00:05:25.283 --> 00:05:26.783
We're saving you, stupid hair balls.

00:05:26.868 --> 00:05:28.827
Not that door. The other door.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:30.954
Hey, hey!

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.415
Any second.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:34.499
[yelps]

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:36.710
- [protestors screaming]
- [guinea pigs squealing]

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.879
[Marmalade grunts]

00:05:39.714 --> 00:05:40.797
[all gasp]

00:05:44.302 --> 00:05:45.927
It's not what it looks like.

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.846
[alarm blaring]

00:05:52.935 --> 00:05:55.353
[Diane] "Trespassing, burglary, mayhem,

00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:58.273
assault with a deadly reptile"?

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:01.234
As if those poor rodents
haven't been through enough already!

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:02.569
No, Diane. Please.

00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:07.157
Whoo! Okay. I'm sorry, Professor,
but I'm calling the chief.

00:06:07.241 --> 00:06:09.367
- Please. Come on.
- [Diane] This experiment is over.

00:06:09.452 --> 00:06:11.787
- [Marmalade] Experiments take time.
- You couldn't help yourself?

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.413
So I had a moment of weakness.
Sue me.

00:06:13.498 --> 00:06:15.165
That's gonna be difficult
to do from prison!

00:06:15.249 --> 00:06:17.334
Guys! What do we do now?

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:22.839
Hmph.
Time to launch a charm offensive.

00:06:22.924 --> 00:06:25.967
Oh, yeah. The full Clooney.

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:29.179
Madam Governor. Diane.

00:06:29.263 --> 00:06:31.473
Do not Clooney me, Wolf.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.683
I see what's going on.
You think I'm still a bad guy

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:36.103
tryin' to bamboozle my way
to freedom.

00:06:36.187 --> 00:06:37.312
But we've changed.

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.023
That flower of goodness
is blossoming all over the place.

00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:42.818
[sighs]
Don't you ever get tired of lying?

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.194
No.

00:06:44.278 --> 00:06:45.362
I mean...

00:06:45.446 --> 00:06:47.864
Fudge.
That was a trick question, right?

00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:50.450
[sighs]
I gave you an opportunity.

00:06:50.535 --> 00:06:52.035
A chance to show the world

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.329
that you're more
than just a scary stereotype,

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:58.917
but you're too proud or too gutless
to take advantage of it.

00:06:59.001 --> 00:07:01.169
Gutless? I'm gutless?

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:03.588
Oh-ho-ho!
I'm sorry, have we met?

00:07:03.673 --> 00:07:05.340
I'm the villain of every story.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.842
Guilty until proven innocent.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.594
Even if by some miracle
we did change,

00:07:09.679 --> 00:07:11.763
who's gonna believe us, huh?

00:07:11.848 --> 00:07:13.557
Of course you wouldn't know
anything about that

00:07:13.641 --> 00:07:16.560
with your Little-Miss-Perfect
power suits.

00:07:17.979 --> 00:07:19.563
Is that so?

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.066
Wait a second, what did...
How did you...

00:07:23.151 --> 00:07:26.528
A wolf and a fox
are not so different.

00:07:28.197 --> 00:07:30.699
Maybe they will believe you,
maybe they won't.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.075
But it doesn't matter.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.828
Don't do it for them.
Do it for you.

00:07:34.912 --> 00:07:37.289
This is a chance
to write your own story,

00:07:37.373 --> 00:07:39.875
to find a better life for you
and your friends.

00:07:41.085 --> 00:07:42.711
Come on,
what have you got to lose?

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.504
I don't know. My dignity?

00:07:46.007 --> 00:07:49.259
Yeah, well,
that ship has already sailed.

00:07:49.343 --> 00:07:50.802
[car door opens]

00:07:55.558 --> 00:07:57.893
Believe it or not,
I'm rootin' for you, Wolf.

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.854
So you're not gonna call the chief?

00:08:02.106 --> 00:08:03.440
I'll see you at the gala.

